<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>
    <!-- ShellUserService extends android.os.Binder (the Shizuku UserService
         pattern), not android.app.Service, so it has no instantiable
         no-arg-constructor contract and lint's Instantiated check fires on it
         even though the Shizuku host DOES instantiate it reflectively via
         ComponentName.

         The ignore path MUST be the manifest, not the Kotlin source. Lint anchors
         this issue to the `<service>` declaration in AndroidManifest.xml, so a
         source-scoped ignore silently fails to suppress anything — and because
         `Instantiatable` is a lint-vital (release) check, that turns into a hard
         `assembleRelease` failure:

             AndroidManifest.xml:85: Error: ShellUserService must extend
             android.app.Service [Instantiatable]

         This was verified by building both ways. The scope is therefore broader
         than ideal (it disables the check for every declared component), but
         narrowing it is not possible while the report is manifest-anchored. If
         the service is ever migrated to a real android.app.Service subclass, this
         suppression should be deleted outright rather than re-scoped. -->
    <issue id="Instantiatable">
        <ignore path="*/AndroidManifest.xml" />
    </issue>
</lint>
